IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rvsa-owner`
IMPORT `rvsa-rules`

-- Road Vehicle Standards Rules 2019 -- worked cases, from the importer's and owner's seat (REQ-0099). Expected values were
-- written by hand from the deposited Rules (Compilation No. 5, F2024C00112) and the Act, never copied from the encoding's
-- output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.

-- A 1996 Nissan Skyline passenger car, applied for in 2026: 30 years, category MA: eligible under s 36.
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle eligible for a concessional approval` `an older vehicle: built at least 25 years before I apply` `a passenger car, forward-control or off-road passenger vehicle, moped, motorcycle, tricycle or light goods vehicle (MA, MB, MC, LA-LE, NA)` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `eligible: the Minister may grant a concessional RAV entry approval if satisfied of the criterion; the approval is also my import approval (ss 35, 146)`
-- A 2005 car (21 years): not under s 36.
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle eligible for a concessional approval` `an older vehicle: built at least 25 years before I apply` `a passenger car, forward-control or off-road passenger vehicle, moped, motorcycle, tricycle or light goods vehicle (MA, MB, MC, LA-LE, NA)` 21 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not eligible under the criterion I named`
-- A 30-year-old bus: the older vehicle criterion covers only the listed categories.
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle eligible for a concessional approval` `an older vehicle: built at least 25 years before I apply` `another category (for example a bus or heavy goods vehicle)` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not eligible under the criterion I named`
-- A specialist vehicle on the SEVs Register, to be modified by a RAW under a Model Report.
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle eligible for a concessional approval` `a specialist or enthusiast vehicle on the SEVs Register (or a used two- or three-wheeler), modified by a registered automotive workshop under an approved Model Report` `a passenger car, forward-control or off-road passenger vehicle, moped, motorcycle, tricycle or light goods vehicle (MA, MB, MC, LA-LE, NA)` 5 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `eligible: the Minister may grant a concessional RAV entry approval if satisfied of the criterion; the approval is also my import approval (ss 35, 146)`
-- Only general suitability: conditional on the Minister (s 41).
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle eligible for a concessional approval` `none of these: only that the Minister is satisfied it is suitable for entry on the RAV` `another category (for example a bus or heavy goods vehicle)` 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `eligible only if the Minister is satisfied the vehicle is suitable for entry on the RAV (s 41)`

-- Personal effects (s 39). Owned in the UK for 18 months before moving; applying 2 months after arrival: met.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the personal effects criterion` TRUE TRUE 18 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Owned only 10 months before arrival: not met.
#ASSERT NOT `Do I meet the personal effects criterion` TRUE TRUE 10 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Applying 7 months after arrival: not met.
#ASSERT NOT `Do I meet the personal effects criterion` TRUE TRUE 18 7 TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle eligible for a concessional approval` `my personal vehicle, owned and used overseas for 12 months before I moved to Australia permanently` `a passenger car, forward-control or off-road passenger vehicle, moped, motorcycle, tricycle or light goods vehicle (MA, MB, MC, LA-LE, NA)` 5 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `eligible: the Minister may grant a concessional RAV entry approval if satisfied of the criterion; the approval is also my import approval (ss 35, 146)`

-- Which import approval.
#ASSERT `Which import approval do I need` `for a temporary stay, not to be used on public roads except in exceptional circumstances` EQUALS `a non-RAV entry import approval, if the Minister is satisfied it will stay temporarily and stay off public roads; it may require me to export it (ss 150, 152, 157)`
#ASSERT `Which import approval do I need` `only for a race or rally, an exhibition of a vehicle not generally available here, filming, testing or market evaluation, or as a hot rod or other significantly modified vehicle, not generally on public roads` EQUALS `a non-RAV entry import approval, if the Minister is satisfied; it may require me to export or destroy it, and limit its use (ss 150, 151, 157)`
#ASSERT `Which import approval do I need` `to bring back my vehicle that is on the RAV (or has an identification plate) and is now outside Australia` EQUALS `a reimportation import approval, if the Secretary is satisfied that I own it and it still matches its RAV entry or plate (ss 162, 163)`

-- Importing. A visiting tourist air-freights a car on a CPD carnet, with no approval: permitted (s 171(2)).
#ASSERT `May I import this vehicle under the Rules` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `on a CPD carnet, with temporary admission under the Private Road Vehicles Convention` EQUALS `yes: a circumstance the rules set out applies (s 22(2)(d))`
-- The same car with no carnet and no approval: not permitted.
#ASSERT `May I import this vehicle under the Rules` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of these` EQUALS `no: importing it would contravene s 22(1), an offence and a civil penalty of up to 120 penalty units`
-- The 1996 Skyline with its concessional approval: permitted as an import approval holder.
#ASSERT `May I import this vehicle under the Rules` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `none of these` EQUALS `yes: I hold an import approval in force that specifies this vehicle (s 22(2)(c))`

-- Providing it. The carnet car lent to a friend, within the Convention's conditions: s 50(2).
#ASSERT `May I provide this vehicle under the Rules` TRUE FALSE FALSE `on a CPD carnet, with temporary admission under the Private Road Vehicles Convention` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: providing it to have work done, to protect, store or transport it, or in a circumstance in the rules, is not caught (s 24(3))`
-- Hired out as a taxi, against the Convention's conditions: not covered by s 50.
#ASSERT `May I provide this vehicle under the Rules` TRUE FALSE FALSE `on a CPD carnet, with temporary admission under the Private Road Vehicles Convention` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: providing it would contravene s 24(1), an offence and a civil penalty of up to 120 penalty units`
-- Handed to the registered workshop the concessional approval names: s 50(6).
#ASSERT `May I provide this vehicle under the Rules` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: providing it to have work done, to protect, store or transport it, or in a circumstance in the rules, is not caught (s 24(3))`

-- Modifying (s 26, s 51). A new ute on the RAV, a canopy fitted before delivery on the type approval holder's written
-- instructions: allowed even though outside the pathway.
#ASSERT `May I modify this vehicle under the Rules` TRUE FALSE TRUE `on the type approval holder's written instructions (type approval pathway vehicle)` EQUALS `yes: the rules allow the modification (s 26(1)(e))`
#ASSERT `May I modify this vehicle under the Rules` TRUE FALSE TRUE `another modification` EQUALS `no: the modification would contravene s 26, an offence and a civil penalty of up to 120 penalty units`
#ASSERT `May I modify this vehicle under the Rules` TRUE TRUE TRUE `another modification` EQUALS `the Act does not restrict it: s 26 applies only before the vehicle is first provided to a consumer in Australia; State or Territory law governs later modifications and use`

-- Conditions as rules (days). Exported on day 80 of a 90-day condition: FULFILLED. On day 120: BREACH.
#TRACE `the export-or-destroy condition` 90 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `I, the approval holder` DOES `export or destroy the vehicle` AT 80
#TRACE `the export-or-destroy condition` 90 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `I, the approval holder` DOES `export or destroy the vehicle` AT 120
